### Full KYC and compliance review (FR-KYC-2 to FR-KYC-4). Fake test data only.
# Prerequisites: run the token requests in auth.http (customer1, officer1, officer2) and the
# customer1 minimum-KYC request there. Infra: postgres, redis, keycloak and localstack from compose.

### customer1: full KYC details -> 201 {status SUBMITTED, requiredDocuments [PAN_CARD, ADDRESS_PROOF]}
# Second run -> 409 KYC_ALREADY_SUBMITTED. Without minimum KYC -> 403 KYC_REQUIRED.
POST {{api}}/api/v1/kyc/full
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"address": "12 Test Street, Indiranagar, Bengaluru 560038"}

> {% client.global.set("kyc_case_id", response.body.id); %}

### customer1: upload the PAN card (any small PNG/JPG/PDF of your own test image) -> 201 {sha256, contentType}
# The type is detected from the file's first bytes, not from its name or Content-Type.
POST {{api}}/api/v1/kyc/cases/{{kyc_case_id}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=kyc

--kyc
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="type"

PAN_CARD
--kyc
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="pan.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./samples/fake-pan.png
--kyc--

> {% client.global.set("kyc_doc_id", response.body.id); %}

### customer1: upload the address proof -> 201
POST {{api}}/api/v1/kyc/cases/{{kyc_case_id}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=kyc

--kyc
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="type"

ADDRESS_PROOF
--kyc
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="address.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./samples/fake-address.pdf
--kyc--

### customer1: a text file renamed to .pdf -> 415 UNSUPPORTED_DOCUMENT_TYPE
POST {{api}}/api/v1/kyc/cases/{{kyc_case_id}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=kyc

--kyc
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="type"

PHOTO
--kyc
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="not-really.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

this is plain text, not a PDF
--kyc--

### officer1: the queue -> 200 {items: [...], page, size, totalElements, totalPages}
GET {{api}}/api/v1/compliance/kyc-cases?status=SUBMITTED&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### officer1: case detail (address in clear, document list)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/compliance/kyc-cases/{{kyc_case_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### officer1: presigned link to the PAN card, valid 5 minutes -> 200 {url, expiresAt}
GET {{api}}/api/v1/compliance/kyc-cases/{{kyc_case_id}}/documents/{{kyc_doc_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### officer1 (maker): verify -> 200 VERIFIED
POST {{api}}/api/v1/compliance/kyc-cases/{{kyc_case_id}}/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### officer1 again as checker -> 409 MAKER_CHECKER_VIOLATION
POST {{api}}/api/v1/compliance/kyc-cases/{{kyc_case_id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### officer2 (checker): approve -> 200 APPROVED; publishes KycLevelUpgraded(FULL)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/compliance/kyc-cases/{{kyc_case_id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{officer2_token}}

### customer1: now FULL
GET {{api}}/api/v1/kyc/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### officer2: reject without a reason -> 400 (on a SUBMITTED or VERIFIED case, with a reason -> 200 REJECTED)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/compliance/kyc-cases/{{kyc_case_id}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{officer2_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}
